  "description": "Recurring oil slick in block Eugene Island 316 off the coast of Louisiana. From 03.08 to 20.09.2026 NOAA/NESDIS analysts saw it every time at the same point and attribute it to a pipeline; the source is not officially confirmed, the US Coast Guard and BSEE are investigating. Slicks are outlined automatically from NISAR L-band images (HH, 40 MHz); the 'oil-likeness' score is a ranking for review, not proof. On the NISAR images of 07.07 and 19.07 a thin plume from the same point is visible before the first report. 'Before' is an image of the same track with no trace at the point: 20.01.2026 for track 156D, 10.07.2026 for 033A.",
